  <result type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved framework conditions for sustainable development</narrative>
   </title>
   <reference code="269640" vocabulary="99"></reference>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">SSC contributions in 2019 to framework conditions within primary healthcare in Mexico: &quot;3 &quot;.

Score from 1-5, 1 lowest and 5 highest.

The planned output targets in the project have partly been met in 2019.

2019 has primarily focused on establishing good relations with the new Mexican Government, who came into power in December 2018. Furthermore, focus was on defining concrete areas of collaboration of the second phase of the SSC in alignment with the new political prioritizations in collaboration with partner authorities. It was an objective to sign the second phase of the SSC. However, this did not happen due to several factors, the main factor being the restructuring of the central administration in Mexico, which has been a longer process than expected.</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2019-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2019-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="5"></target>
     <actual value="3"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
